  "comment": "The vectors pinning Prima.DeviceCert and its challenge and proof: every side re-signs each certificate whose signer is named and reproduces its sig, checks each certificate under the named key's public key with the given home, clock (Unix milliseconds), clock tolerance and current key_epoch, and reaches the named result or refusal; refuses each malformed certificate and challenge; and holds each proof to the challenge held for the connection at the given time, a mismatch naming the first field that differs in the order purpose, home, athanor, client_id, device_key, nonce, expires_at. Expiry is strict: at or after expires_at a certificate is refused whatever the tolerance, which applies to not_before only. A local subject names one home as issuer and audience and needs no identifier or key_epoch. A challenge lives lifetime_ms from issue. A pair challenge binds the prospective client id the pairing invitation reserved; a proof of one purpose is refused for every other.",
